// A Transfer is permitted if EITHER its amount is under 100 OR the same
// user logged in within the last 30 minutes. The `||` disjoins a native
// Cedar comparison with a `temporal { … }` monitor in one expression, so
// the rule fires whenever either side holds and is silent only when both
// fail. Exercises the OR truth table for a hoisted temporal conjunct
// sitting beside native Cedar.
permit (
    principal,
    action == Drupe::Action::"Transfer",
    resource
)
when {
    context.input.amount < 100
    || temporal {
        formerly within 30m Drupe::Action::"Login"::request{ input.user: context.input.user }
    }
};
